Change: Fetch the app info of all enabled apps with one cache request

With Redis as local cache, every first access to the info of an app in a request
was its own network request, about 60 per request (one for the app id and one
for the path of info.xml per enabled app). They are now fetched together with
one MGET on the first access. The etag check of info.xml on every lookup stays
as it was; caches without multi-get and any error fall back to single reads.

Measured on a SaaS test instance (Redis requests per page, warm cache): login
page 301 before, 13 after; files page 653 / 37; PROPFIND 360 / 8; capabilities
400 / 10. Part of this comes from the request cache of #118.
